## OPSEC & Evasion Techniques

### Detection Risks

- **Process creation alerts** - DumpIt.exe execution
- **Large file creation** - Multi-GB dump files
- **LSASS process access** - Memory reading attempts
- **Unusual memory usage** - Significant RAM consumption

### Evasion Strategies

- **Use legitimate tools** - Task Manager, built-in utilities
- **Process hollowing** - Hide malicious activity in legitimate processes
- **Direct system calls** - Bypass API monitoring
- **Memory-only execution** - Avoid disk artifacts

### Alternative Methods

```bash
# Alternative: Living off the land with built-in tools
rundll32.exe C:\Windows\System32\comsvcs.dll, MiniDump [LSASS_PID] C:\temp\lsass.dmp full

# PowerShell method (requires admin)
Get-Process lsass | Out-Minidump -DumpFilePath C:\temp\lsass.dmp
```

<div class="warning-box" markdown="1">
**Modern EDR:** Many endpoint solutions now monitor LSASS access attempts and memory dumps
</div>

